WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:03.595
Unit twenty. Events in Coding!

2
00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:09.181
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:12.291
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.341 --> 00:00:16.035
Today we learn about Events in Coding. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.451
Event. Say it with me. Event!

6
00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:28.634
Click. Say it with me. Click!

7
00:00:32.101 --> 00:00:36.301
Key press. Say it with me. Key press!

8
00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:43.664
Trigger. Say it with me. Trigger!

9
00:00:47.169 --> 00:00:51.102
Action. Say it with me. Action!

10
00:00:54.572 --> 00:00:57.905
Code. Say it with me. Code!

11
00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:05.360
Sprite. Say it with me. Sprite!

12
00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:13.103
Respond. Say it with me. Respond!

13
00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:29.199
An event is something that happens, like a click or a key press. In code, an event can trigger an action. For example, when I click a sprite, it can respond by jumping.

14
00:01:29.249 --> 00:01:32.513
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:33.258 --> 00:01:38.731
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:40.029
Key press!

17
00:01:41.231 --> 00:01:46.663
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:47.863
Sprite!

19
00:01:48.937 --> 00:01:56.415
Did you know? Almost every button you press on a website runs code triggered by an event!

20
00:01:56.465 --> 00:01:58.882
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:59.581 --> 00:02:07.912
Think and answer. What event would make your game start?

22
00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:09.159
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.186 --> 00:02:15.877
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:19.255
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

